 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No plate in 25 (breaking the covenant, the curse, the evil abode). Wheat for «يبسط الرزق لمن يشاء ويقدر», a falling leaf for «وفرحوا بالحياة الدنيا… إلا متاع». STAGING v4: c1 (25): a home by day; three men in dark robes stand apart from their relatives, who sit on the left (both tafsirs: they cut what Allah ordered joined, kinship among it). A seal plate for the covenant of Allah that draws back (undraw) as they break it (25:3-7); they shake their heads (25:2, breaking it: As-Sa'di, they met it with turning away) and turn their backs on the relatives (25:8, they cut). The camera holds on the dark-robed men for they spread corruption (25:15; no act of corruption is drawn) and through the curse and the evil abode (25:18-23): nothing of the Hereafter is drawn and nobody leaves on those words. c2 (26): a market by day; a rich man and a poor man: the camera closes on the rich man as He extends provision (26:3, wheat plate) and on the poor man as He restricts (26:6); wide for they rejoice in the worldly life (26:7: the disbelievers, not drawn as anyone in particular), a falling-leaf plate for the brief enjoyment (26:8). The cover now shows the dark-robed men (25:15)."
